worktree: ../okay-wt-proto
spec: specs/di.md (lifetimes), docs/di.md

why: an instance per CONSUMER needs a named trait per capability today,
  and the pure and the releasing shapes have different types — so a
  provider that starts closing its instances breaks every consumer.
  A consumer must not know whether what it asks for is closed.

what: core — `New[A]` (one type, `apply(): A ! Resource`), `fresh[A]`
  as the consumer one-liner, `prototype` in two spellings mirroring
  Module.value/module; `Resource.scoped` for the per-call region that
  is spelled with two type arguments today. Tests including the claim
  that the CALL SITE does not change when the provider adds a release.
  docs/di.md gains the three lifetimes, samples compiled in TestDiDocs.

next: New/fresh/prototype, then scoped, then the docs
